# Reading: Shifting Through the Neck (repertoire plan: st-read-shifting). An original 32-bar
# reading study that climbs the neck through five positions, each with its own key and meter:
#   bars 1-8    E major (4 sharps), 4/4, position I   (open strings, finger 1 on fret 1)
#   bars 9-14   F minor (4 flats), 3/4, position V    (finger 1 on fret 5)
#   bars 15-20  C major, 6/8, position VII            (finger 1 on fret 7)
#   bars 21-26  A major (3 sharps), 3/4, position IX  (finger 1 on fret 9)
#   bars 27-32  E major again, 4/4, position XII      (the first section an octave higher)
# The keys move by major thirds and their neighbours: E to F minor through the common note
# G# = Ab, F minor ends on its dominant C, which becomes the new tonic; C turns to A minor and
# its dominant E, then A major, whose last chord B7 leads home to E.
# Every shift has a way in: an open string (bars 8, 26), the same note on a new string
# (bars 14-15) or a finger that changes on a held note (bar 20). Fingerings are given only at
# the shifts. The eighth note keeps its speed through every change of meter.
title: Reading: Shifting Through the Neck
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original reading study through the positions
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 9
